const e={"seo.purpose":"Who the leave planner is for","seo.purpose.p1":"Use it when you already know how many days you can take and want to see which 2026 or 2027 dates connect.","seo.purpose.p2":"It is for lining up annual leave beside Lunar New Year, Dragon Boat Festival, or a long weekend.","seo.why":"Why use this planner","seo.why.p1":"It uses the same Taiwan government calendar as the day calculator on this site, checked against the DGPA notices.","seo.why.li1":"Each row is one option. Do not add the rows together.","seo.why.li2":"The combined plan starts only after you type a number, and it never spends the same date twice.","seo.why.li3":"The page says this is the government calendar. A company notice comes first.","seo.why.p2":"The dates are calculated in your browser.","seo.faq":"Leave planner questions","seo.faq.q1":"Does this calculate my legal leave balance?","seo.faq.q1a":"No. You type how many days you still have. The page only places those days on the calendar.","seo.faq.q2":"Is it true that 2027 has no makeup workdays?","seo.faq.q2a":"The DGPA notice for 2027 lists extra days off and no makeup workdays, matching the rule that stopped makeup shifts. A company can still announce its own.","seo.faq.q3":"Why can’t I add every row?","seo.faq.q3a":"Rows can share a date. Adding them would count that day twice. Use the combined plan to schedule more than one bridge.","seo.faq.q4":"What if I leave the number blank?","seo.faq.q4a":"You can still read the single options. The combined plan waits for a number."};export{e as default};
